      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since tcpc_alert_event() is an interrupt handler there\u0027s no guarantee that it will get called strictly after the ADC module init hook.\n\nWe could also change the ADC init hook priority so it runs before the PD hooks which trigger TCPC alert events, but that\u0027s done in common code so we couldn\u0027t merge it.\n\nIf I call board_get_version() from within tcpc_alert_event() then the EC will crash with a timeout caused by spending too much time spent in interrupt context.\n\nThis approach seemed the least bad IMO, but I\u0027m open to ideas.",
